comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T14:58:07.343Z","harness:codex","Final evidence: the replication manifest contains an exact CLI-owned refusal census (76 across 12 files), zero-waiver policy, stable shared refusal codes, and fail-closed drift tests. This tranche moves get selector and author-coordinate policy into SDK-owned primitives and makes future partial migration visible in quality:static."
  "2026-08-07T14:58:58.550Z","harness:codex","Closeout boundary: this broad PR materially advances the item but does not satisfy its every-rule acceptance criterion. The live census remains 76 CLI-owned refusals, so the item is returned to open and released rather than falsely closed. Future work can now use the exact gate as its ratchet."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T14:58:07.798Z","harness:codex","A refusal-migration roadmap needs an executable residual census, not only a desired end state. Exact file/count drift makes remaining CLI ownership explicit without pretending the entire historical backlog vanished in one change."
